# Frequency data

`data/frequency.json` is a derived word-count table used as the ranking prior for
`upodesh`.

## Source

Counts are derived from the **IndicCorp V2** Bengali corpus
(`bn.txt`, ~15.9 GB, one sentence per line), part of the AI4Bharat
`ai4bharat/IndicCorpV2` dataset on Hugging Face. Only tokens matching
dictionary words are kept (99,422 / 159,384 = 62.4%, from 922M tokens).

Corpus provenance:

- Dataset: `ai4bharat/IndicCorpV2` (Hugging Face)
- Benchmark paper: Doddapaneni et al. (2023), *Towards Leaving No Indic
  Language Behind: Building Monolingual Corpora, Benchmark and Models for
  Indic Languages*, ACL 2023 (arXiv:2112.02972), doi:10.18653/v1/2023.acl-long.693
- Corpus file sha256:
  `a5b0ec3df504ebcadf551249c6dc53c9ab17112739aedfa861b52e6b7b2f2d6d`

## Licence

IndicCorp V2 is made available under the **Creative Commons CC-0**
assignment of creators' rights (public domain dedication):

<https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/>

The dataset card states that datasets created as part of this work are
released under CC-0 and models/code under MIT. The derived counts here
are CC-0-clean; this attribution exists for citation and provenance.

## Attribution

> Doddapaneni, S., Aralikatte, R., Ramesh, G., Goyal, S., Khapra, M. M.,
> Kunchukuttan, A., et al. (2023): *Towards Leaving No Indic Language
> Behind: Building Monolingual Corpora, Benchmark and Models for Indic
> Languages.* Proceedings of the 61st Annual Meeting of the Association
> for Computational Linguistics (ACL 2023).

Data: AI4Bharat IndicCorp V2, distributed by the IndicNLP project.

## Regenerating

```sh
cargo run --release --manifest-path generate/Cargo.toml --bin corpus-count -- \
    --corpus /tmp/opencode/bn.txt --out data/frequency.json
```
